  "description": "AGSC-01-19: build.out MUST NOT name content/, which a build never writes, or dist/, which is generated, or a path under either, its first segment compared ASCII case-insensitively; a value that does is AGSC-E204. A trailing / is accepted and stripped. Each sub-case runs `build` over a scratch copy of the minimal fixture, with SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH set and no git history: four project files whose build.out is content, dist, Content/site and dist/www, and the same value content given as the environment value AGSC_BUILD_OUT, which sets build.out through the environment layer. Each is refused with an error finding AGSC-E204 and writes no file anywhere in the Bundle, so the source tree is never overwritten; the exit code is 1 or 2 (an error finding, or a configuration fault, AGSC-09-08). The control www/ builds, exits 0, reports no AGSC-E204 and writes only under www/.",
